  "exhibits": [
    {
      "id": "aud-m2-tbs2-ex1",
      "title": "Process narrative",
      "html": "<p>Sales staff can create customers and approve their own credit limits. Shipments are entered through a system with a documented matching control. Developers can alter that control directly in production. The outsourced billing provider supplied only a SOC 1 Type 1 report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "aud-m2-tbs2-ex2",
      "title": "Audit objective",
      "html": "<p>The team wants to rely on relevant controls throughout the year. A single observed transaction matched successfully. No testing over the period has been performed.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Concern in customer and credit approval</h3><p>Self-approval weakens independent authorization.</p><h3>Concern in production program access</h3><p>Developers could bypass authorized and tested changes.</p><h3>What the Type 1 report does not establish</h3><p>Type 1 is an at-a-date design report.</p><h3>Additional evidence for planned reliance</h3><p>Planned reliance requires evidence across the relevant period.</p>"
